# G8 (graphics): the mouse on the menus in graphics. Places are pixels of the 640 by 480 screen (the titles and items are where the painter's
# geometry puts them with the test font). Open a menu, hover its items, hover another title to switch, click a greyed item (nothing),
# run an item with a click, drag from the View title through to Ruler and release (it runs), click away to close, hold the button on a
# title and slide to an item, then the keys on a menu the pointer opened. Played on the host through quill-paint's Gfx, and into
# QUILLDOS.EXE from a QUILL_MOUSE file, so every frame's CRC-32 must be equal in both graphics modes.
@copy letter.rtf
@open LETTER.RTF
@click 57 9             # Edit opens
@move 113 148           # Select All lit
@move 145 9             # hovering the Find title switches menus
@click 57 9             # back to Edit
@click 113 80           # Cut is greyed: nothing, the menu stays
@click 113 148          # Select All runs
@drag 387 9 428 72      # View title through to Ruler, release: the ruler goes
@drag 387 9 428 72      # and comes back
@click 57 9
@click 500 300          # a click away closes the menu and does nothing else
@down 387 9             # held on a title: its menu shows
@move 428 54            # slid to Toolbar, lit
@up 387 30              # let go on the menu's frame: nothing runs, the menu stays
@click 600 300          # closed by a click outside
@click 57 9
down down
esc
f10 end enter
